<main id="main"><section class="research-hero"><div><p class="eyebrow">Mechanical Design · Work in Progress</p><h1>Continuum Manipulator</h1><p class="subtitle">Lifting Dynamics Analysis</p><p class="hero-intro">Developing a single-section, three-tendon continuum manipulator to investigate how payload and motion affect lifting behavior.</p><div class="research-meta"><span>Fall 2026 – Present</span><span>Duke University · Team course project</span></div><p class="status">In progress · Updated November 2026</p><div class="hero-actions"><a class="button primary" href="#contributions">My contributions ↓</a><a class="button" href="#next">Next steps ↓</a></div></div><aside class="focus-panel"><p class="eyebrow">Design Question</p><h2>Load-dependent deformation</h2><p>How do payload, arm configuration, and lifting speed affect the behavior of a tendon-driven flexible arm?</p></aside></section>
<section class="section dark" id="contributions"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">01</p><h2>My Contributions</h2></div><p>Current scope and contributions.</p></div><div class="contribution-list"><div><span>01</span><p>Collaborating on the development of a single-section, three-tendon continuum arm with a rigid fixture and simple hook or payload attachment.</p></div><div><span>02</span><p>Developing the modeling and experimental approach for studying body deformation, positioning accuracy, stability, and usable lifting capacity.</p></div></div></section>
<section class="section split" id="next"><div><p class="eyebrow">02</p><h2>Next Development Steps</h2></div><div class="copy"><p>The planned evaluation includes deflection, tracking error, overshoot, settling time, repeatability, and sustained-load behavior. These are evaluation objectives; measured performance and validated load limits are not yet reported.</p><div class="callout"><strong>Project scope</strong><p>This page describes the lifting-dynamics course study. The separate gripper and wrist development is outside the scope of this case study.</p></div></div></section>
